On Sat, Jun 1, 2013 at 2:49 AM, Jacob Errington <nictytan@gmail.com> wrote:

> If we decide to refactor the connective system, could {gi mu'i} be made to
> mean the same thing as the clunky {gi'e mu'i bo} (which under GIJA would be
> {gi je mu'i bo} ?
>


No, because one of "ge (broda gi-mu'i brode) gi (mu'i brodi)" and "ge
(broda) gi (mu'i brode gi-mu'i brodi)" would be inaccessible.


> I can see this breaking the case where {broda gi'e mu'i brode}. However,
> maybe if we throw in a {bo}, everything becomes okay? e.g. {.i broda
> gimu'ibo brode}. I think this works, and doesn't break anything.
>
> Thoughts?
>

 I think that one should work.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

